<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-MICHAEL SCHUMACHER WINS FRENCH GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-MICHAEL SCHUMACHER WINS FRENCH GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>MAGNY-COURS, France 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Schumacher of Germany, driving a Ferrari, won the French Grand Prix motor race on Sunday.  </p>
<p>Heinz-Harald Frentzen of Germany finished second in a</p>
<p>Williams, with Britain's Eddie Irvine third in a Ferrari.</p>
<p>Jacques Villeneuve of Canada finished fourth in a Williams,</p>
<p>with Jean Alesi of France fifth in a Benetton and Ralf</p>
<p>Schumacher of Germany sixth in a Jordan.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after eight rounds):</p>
<p>  1. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    47</p>
<p>  2. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)	     33</p>
<p>  3. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany)	 19</p>
<p>  4. Eddie Irvine (Britain)		    18</p>
<p>  5 equal. Olivier Panis (France)	    15</p>
<p>  5 equal. Jean Alesi (France)		 15</p>
<p>  7. David Coulthard (Britain)		 11</p>
<p>  8 equal. Gerhard Berger  (Germany)	 10</p>
<p>  8 equal. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   10</p>
<p> 10. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)	     8</p>
<p> 11. Johnny Herbert (Britain)		   7</p>
<p> 12. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)		6</p>
<p> 13. Ralf Schumacher (Germany)		  5</p>
<p> 14. Mika Salo (Finland)			  2</p>
<p> 15. Nicola Larini (Italy)			1</p>
<p> 16. Shinji Nakano (Japan)			1</p>
<p>Constructors' championship:</p>
<p>  1. Ferrari					 65 points</p>
<p>  2. Williams					52</p>
<p>  3. Benetton					25</p>
<p>  4. McLaren					 21</p>
<p>  5. Prost					   16</p>
<p>  6. Jordan					  13</p>
<p>  7. Sauber					   8</p>
<p>  8. Stewart					  6</p>
<p>  9. Tyrrell					  2</p>
